      "body": "Both files untouched \u2014 old `target_modules` still there, `utils.py` still has 2 candidates.\n\n## Why I brought up the config\n\nTwo separate things got tangled in my last message. Splitting them:\n\n**You need ZERO config changes to make your notebook run.** Your YAML is already fine for the 2D task. I bundled the config in because your workshop instructions said \"reconcile any changes you have made\" \u2014 and that one line is the last leftover of the LoRA patch. But it's a *training-quality* issue, not a crash. It's optional and separate. Skip it for now if you want the notebook working first.\n\nIf you do want it later, it's one line, line 148:\n```yaml\ntarget_modules: [fc1, fc2, attn.qkv, attn.proj]\n```\n(`q_proj`/`k_proj`/`v_proj`/`out_proj` are HuggingFace names that don't exist in Surya, so they're silently ignored and attention never gets adapted. `fc1`/`fc2` do match, which is why nothing errors.)\n\nSame for `workshop_infrastructure/utils.py` \u2014 **optional**, and it's shared workshop code, so your call. Skipping it just means your first plot looks like noise instead of a Sun; I gave you a notebook-only cell that does the same job without touching it.\n\n## What you actually need to change \u2014 notebook only, 6 spots\n\n| Cell | Change | Required? |\n|---|---|---|\n| **17** | Drop `num_outputs=1` \u2192 add `ft_out_chans=len(cfg.data.channels)`, `ft_unembedding_type=\"linear\"` | **Yes \u2014 this is your crash** |\n| **13** | Uncomment (defines `batch` for later cells) | Yes |\n| **23** | Uncomment (defines `output`) | Yes |\n| **25** | `downstream_apps.template.metrics.template_metrics` \u2192 `downstream_apps.flare_forecast.metrics.flare_metrics` | Yes |\n| **28/30/32** | `batch[\"forecast\"]` \u2192 `batch[\"forecast\"][:, :, 0].float()` | Yes |\n| **new cell + 38** | `Flare2DLightningModule` class, then swap the name in 38 | Yes \u2014 training breaks otherwise |\n| **19** | Append the decoder-recovery snippet | No \u2014 but your plot is noise without it |\n| **new cell** | `plot_prediction(...)` | That's the thing you asked for |\n\nCell 17 alone fixes the error you hit. The rest is what breaks *next* as you run downward.\n\nWant me to just apply the notebook changes directly so you don't have to hand-copy eight cells? I'd touch only `2_finetune_2D-image-flip.ipynb` and nothing else \u2014 no config, no shared files.",
