            },
            "raw_output": "=== s3 cache path derivation ===\n22:import hashlib\n71:def _resolve_s3_mode(s3_mode, s3_download_to_temp, s3_use_simplecache) -> str:\n74:    ``s3_download_to_temp`` and ``s3_use_simplecache`` are the legacy API. They were\n76:    dispatch, so setting ``s3_use_simplecache=True`` silently did nothing. They are\n79:    legacy_used = s3_download_to_temp is not None or s3_use_simplecache is not None\n83:            \"Pass either s3_mode or the deprecated s3_download_to_temp/s3_use_simplecache \"\n85:            f\"{s3_download_to_temp!r}, s3_use_simplecache={s3_use_simplecache!r}).\"\n90:        # and won over simplecache.\n94:        elif s3_use_simplecache:\n95:            resolved = \"simplecache\"\n99:            \"s3_download_to_temp/s3_use_simplecache are deprecated; use \"\n112:            \"  download    \u2014 whole-object download to s3_cache_dir, then open locally (recommended)\\n\"\n113:            \"  simplecache \u2014 fsspec read-through cache into s3_cache_dir\\n\"\n114:            \"  stream      \u2014 direct s3fs handle, no local cache (unreliable for NetCDF/HDF5)\"\n189:        data: Normalized array of shape (C, H, W).\n190:        means: Per-channel means, shape (C,).\n191:        stds: Per-channel standard deviations, shape (C,).\n192:        sl_scale_factors: Per-channel amplitude scaling factors, shape (C,).\n193:        epsilons: Per-channel small constants that prevent division by zero, shape (C,).\n196:        Reconstructed array of shape (C, H, W), dtype float32.\n198:    C, H, W = data.shape\n226:        data: NumPy array of shape (C, H, W).\n227:        means: Per-channel means, shape (C,).\n228:        stds: Per-channel standard deviations, shape (C,).\n229:        sl_scale_factors: Per-channel amplitude scaling factors, shape (C,).\n230:        epsilons: Per-channel small constants that prevent division by zero, shape (C,).\n233:        Normalized array of shape (C, H, W).\n235:    means = means.reshape(*means.shape, 1, 1)\n236:    stds = stds.reshape(*stds.shape, 1, 1)\n237:    sl_scale_factors = sl_scale_factors.reshape(*sl_scale_factors.shape, 1, 1)\n238:    epsilons = epsilons.reshape(*epsilons.shape, 1, 1)\n254:        data: NumPy array of shape (H, W).\n261:        Reconstructed array of shape (H, W).\n297:            input_tensor: Array of shape (C, T, H, W).\n300:            Masked array of the same shape.\n302:        C, T, H, W = input_tensor.shape\n365:            - ``\"download\"`` (default) \u2014 fetch the whole object into ``s3_cache_dir`` with boto3\n368:            - ``\"simplecache\"`` \u2014 fsspec read-through cache into ``s3_cache_dir``.\n369:            - ``\"stream\"`` \u2014 direct s3fs handle; nothing is written to disk and ``s3_cache_dir``\n374:        s3_cache_dir: **Required unless ``s3_mode=\"stream\"``.** Local directory where S3 files are\nShell cwd was reset to /home/jovyan/tmp/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/flare_forecast/old-chats-notebooks",
