            "diffs": [
              {
                "path": "/home/jovyan/tmp/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/flare_forecast/prewarm_cache.py",
                "new_text": "\"\"\"\nPre-download the S3 files a training run will ask for, before the run starts.\n\nWhy this exists\n---------------\nWith ``s3_mode: download``, HelioNetCDFDataset fetches each ~0.5 GB NetCDF file from S3\nthe first time a sample needs it. A 2-frame-input, 1-frame-target sample therefore costs\nthree downloads (~1.6 GB) on its first visit. When that happens inside the training loop\nthe GPU sits idle waiting for the network, which shows up in WandB as a flat GPU-utilization\ntrace with one brief spike per step.\n\nDownloads are network-bound and parallelize well; training is GPU-bound. Running them\nconcurrently through one DataLoader worker gets the worst of both. So: warm the cache here\nfirst (many threads, no GPU, no model in memory), then train against local disk.\n\nThis writes to exactly the paths HelioNetCDFDataset._s3_cache_path() computes, so the\ndataset finds and reuses them. Nothing in workshop_infrastructure/ is modified.\n\nUsage\n-----\n    P=/home/jovyan/envs/surya_ws/bin/python\n\n    # What would be downloaded for the first 150 training samples? (no network traffic)\n    $P -m downstream_apps.flare_forecast.prewarm_cache --split train --n 150 --dry-run\n\n    # Actually warm them, 16 parallel downloads\n    $P -m downstream_apps.flare_forecast.prewarm_cache --split train --n 150 --workers 16\n\n    # Warm the validation samples from specific years (e.g. cycle-24 max vs cycle 25)\n    $P -m downstream_apps.flare_forecast.prewarm_cache --split val --years 2014 2015 2023\n\nPick the SAME --split/--n/--sample/--years you will use for the run, or you will warm\nfiles the run never asks for.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport threading\nimport time\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor, as_completed\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom workshop_infrastructure.configs import load_config\nfrom workshop_infrastructure.utils import make_s3_client, detect_ec2_region, parse_s3_uri\n\nHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\nDEFAULT_CONFIG = os.path.join(HERE, \"configs\", \"config_script.yaml\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cache path \u2014 must stay byte-identical to HelioNetCDFDataset._s3_cache_path()\n# (workshop_infrastructure/datasets/helio.py:840). Verified against files already\n# on disk; see --dry-run output, which reports how many are already present.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef s3_cache_path(s3_uri: str, cache_dir: str) -> str:\n    bucket, key = parse_s3_uri(s3_uri)\n    base = os.path.basename(key) or \"object\"\n    base_safe = re.sub(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]+\", \"_\", base).strip(\"._-\") or \"object\"\n    _, ext = os.path.splitext(base_safe)\n    suffix = ext if ext else \".nc\"\n    key_hash = hashlib.sha1(f\"{bucket}/{key}\".encode()).hexdigest()\n    fname = f\"{bucket}__{key_hash}__{base_safe}\"\n    if not fname.endswith(suffix):\n        fname += suffix\n    return os.path.join(cache_dir, fname)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Work out which timesteps the dataset will actually request.\n#\n# This mirrors two things: HelioNetCDFDataset's validity rule (a reference timestep is\n# usable only if every input offset and the target offset are present in the index) and\n# flare_Dataset's merge_asof + de-duplicate + tolerance matching against the flare\n# catalog. Reproducing them here \u2014 rather than instantiating the dataset \u2014 keeps this\n# script free of scalers, torch and S3 setup, so it starts instantly.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef reference_timesteps(cfg, index_path: str, years: list[int] | None) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    idx = pd.read_csv(index_path, parse_dates=[\"timestep\"])\n    idx = idx[idx[\"present\"] == 1]\n    present = set(idx[\"timestep\"])\n\n    offsets = sorted(cfg.data.time_delta_input_minutes) + [cfg.data.time_delta_target_minutes]\n    offsets = sorted(set(offsets))\n\n    valid = [\n        t for t in sorted(present)\n        if all((t + pd.Timedelta(minutes=o)) in present for o in offsets)\n    ]\n    if not valid:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"No reference timestep in {index_path} has all offsets {offsets}.\")\n\n    flares = pd.read_csv(cfg.data.flare_index_path)\n    flares[\"ds_index\"] = pd.to_datetime(flares[cfg.data.ds_time_column])\n    flares = flares.sort_values(\"ds_index\")\n\n    matched = pd.merge_asof(\n        pd.DataFrame({\"valid_indices\": pd.DatetimeIndex(valid)}),\n        flares[[\"ds_index\", \"GOES_class\", \"CMX\"]],\n        left_on=\"valid_indices\",\n        right_on=\"ds_index\",\n        direction=cfg.data.ds_match_direction,\n    )\n    matched[\"delta\"] = (matched[\"ds_index\"] - matched[\"valid_indices\"]).abs()\n    matched = (matched.sort_values([\"ds_index\", \"delta\"])\n                      .drop_duplicates(\"ds_index\", keep=\"first\"))\n    if cfg.data.ds_time_tolerance is not None:\n        matched = matched[matched[\"delta\"] <= pd.Timedelta(cfg.data.ds_time_tolerance)]\n\n    # flare_Dataset orders samples by flare peak time, and max_number_of_samples takes a\n    # plain [:N] slice of that order \u2014 so \"first N\" here means the N earliest flares.\n    matched = matched.sort_values(\"ds_index\").reset_index(drop=True)\n    if years:\n        matched = matched[matched[\"valid_indices\"].dt.year.isin(years)].reset_index(drop=True)\n    return matched, idx, offsets\n\n\ndef files_for(matched: pd.DataFrame, idx: pd.DataFrame, offsets: list[int]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Every distinct S3 URI the selected samples will touch.\"\"\"\n    path_of = dict(zip(idx[\"timestep\"], idx[\"path\"]))\n    uris = {\n        path_of[t + pd.Timedelta(minutes=o)]\n        for t in matched[\"valid_indices\"]\n        for o in offsets\n    }\n    return sorted(uris)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Download\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n_print_lock = threading.Lock()\n\n\ndef download(client, s3_uri: str, dest: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Download to a unique temp name then rename, so a killed job never leaves a\n    truncated file that the dataset would later open and fail on.\"\"\"\n    bucket, key = parse_s3_uri(s3_uri)\n    tmp = f\"{dest}.{os.getpid()}.{threading.get_ident()}.part\"\n    client.download_file(bucket, key, tmp)\n    os.replace(tmp, dest)\n    return os.path.getsize(dest)\n\n\ndef main(argv=None) -> int:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__,\n                                formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--config\", default=DEFAULT_CONFIG)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--split\", choices=[\"train\", \"val\"], default=\"train\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=None,\n                    help=\"Warm only the first N samples (matches max_number_of_samples).\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--years\", type=int, nargs=\"*\", default=None,\n                    help=\"Restrict to reference timesteps in these years.\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=16, help=\"Parallel downloads.\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--dry-run\", action=\"store_true\",\n                    help=\"Report what is missing and how much it would transfer, then stop.\")\n    args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n\n    cfg = load_config(args.config)\n    cache_dir = cfg.data.s3_cache_dir\n    if not cache_dir:\n        raise SystemExit(\"data.s3_cache_dir is not set in the config; nothing to warm.\")\n    os.makedirs(cache_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n    index_path = cfg.data.train_data_path if args.split == \"train\" else cfg.data.valid_data_path\n    matched, idx, offsets = reference_timesteps(cfg, index_path, args.years)\n\n    total_available = len(matched)\n    if args.n is not None:\n        matched = matched.iloc[: args.n]\n\n    uris = files_for(matched, idx, offsets)\n    todo = [(u, p) for u in uris if not os.path.exists(p := s3_cache_path(u, cache_dir))]\n\n    print(f\"split          : {args.split}  ({index_path})\")\n    print(f\"input offsets  : {offsets} minutes\")\n    print(f\"samples        : {len(matched)} selected of {total_available} available\"\n          + (f\"  (years {args.years})\" if args.years else \"\"))\n    if len(matched):\n        print(f\"date range     : {matched['valid_indices'].min()} -> {matched['valid_indices'].max()}\")\n        mx = matched[matched[\"CMX\"].isin([\"M\", \"X\"])]\n        print(f\"M/X flares     : {len(mx)}\")\n    print(f\"distinct files : {len(uris)}\")\n    print(f\"already cached : {len(uris) - len(todo)}\")\n    print(f\"to download    : {len(todo)}  (~{len(todo) * 0.54:.0f} GB at ~0.54 GB/file)\")\n    print(f\"cache dir      : {cache_dir}\")\n\n    if args.dry_run or not todo:\n        if not todo:\n            print(\"\\nCache is already warm for this selection.\")\n        return 0\n\n    region = (os.environ.get(\"AWS_REGION\") or os.environ.get(\"AWS_DEFAULT_REGION\")\n              or detect_ec2_region())\n    client = make_s3_client(anon=bool(cfg.data.s3_anon), region=region,\n                            pool_size=max(32, args.workers * 2), max_attempts=10)\n\n    print(f\"\\nDownloading with {args.workers} threads...\\n\")\n    t0, done, nbytes, failed = time.perf_counter(), 0, 0, []\n    with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=args.workers) as pool:\n        futures = {pool.submit(download, client, u, p): u for u, p in todo}\n        for fut in as_completed(futures):\n            uri = futures[fut]\n            try:\n                nbytes += fut.result()\n            except Exception as exc:                      # keep going; report at the end\n                failed.append((uri, repr(exc)))\n            done += 1\n            el = time.perf_counter() - t0\n            with _print_lock:\n                rate = nbytes / el / 2**20 if el else 0\n                eta = (len(todo) - done) * el / done if done else 0\n                print(f\"\\r  {done}/{len(todo)}  {nbytes/2**30:6.1f} GB  \"\n                      f\"{rate:6.1f} MB/s  eta {eta/60:5.1f} min  \"\n                      f\"({len(failed)} failed)\", end=\"\", flush=True)\n\n    el = time.perf_counter() - t0\n    print(f\"\\n\\nDone: {done - len(failed)}/{len(todo)} files, {nbytes/2**30:.1f} GB \"\n          f\"in {el/60:.1f} min ({nbytes/el/2**20:.0f} MB/s average).\")\n    if failed:\n        print(f\"\\n{len(failed)} failed \u2014 rerun to retry just these:\")\n        for uri, err in failed[:10]:\n            print(f\"  {uri}  {err}\")\n        return 1\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n"
