    {
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "id": "6be76200-11e1-4e5b-9a06-250c9ea02c8d",
      "time": 1789650314.4411068,
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "Notebook edited \u2014 50 \u2192 56 cells, validates cleanly. Three insertions, each with a plain-English markdown header above it.\n\n## What's new\n\n**Cells 14\u201315 \u2014 speed check (run this first)**\nWalks every sample twice: pass 1 downloads from S3 and leaves the files cached, pass 2 reads from local disk. It prints seconds-per-sample for both and the ratio.\n\nTwo things come out of it. The cache ends up warm, so training isn't waiting on the network. And the cold/warm ratio tells you which resource you're short of: much faster warm means S3 was the bottleneck (that's your flat WandB GPU trace), roughly the same means the GPU is genuinely the limit.\n\n**Cells 22\u201323 \u2014 the missing decoder weights**\nSits between \"load weights\" and the LoRA cell, which is the only place it can go \u2014 the LoRA cell renames every parameter. It copies the two final-layer tensors the loader silently skips (the `157 / 159`), and asserts instead of warning, since a quiet miss is the exact bug being fixed. Expect it to print `unembed.unembed.0.weight -> head_unembed.unembed.0.weight (3328, 1280, 1, 1)`. 3328 = 16\u00d716 patch pixels \u00d7 13 channels, which confirms it's really the image decoder.\n\n**Cells 26\u201327 \u2014 forced flip pass + timing**\nTakes one sample, pushes it through the model upright and vertically flipped (`axis=-2`, same as `flare_dataset.py:151`), on the GPU at batch size 1. It moves only `ts`/`time_delta_input`/`lead_time_delta` to the card, which keeps the ~0.9 GB target tensor off-device for the forward-only part.\n\nIt prints five numbers:\n- **flipped/upright time ratio** \u2014 should be ~1.00. The model does identical arithmetic regardless of pixel values, so a ratio near 1 is the *correct* answer, not a failed test.\n- **error vs ground truth** and **error of just copying the last input forward**. That second one is the persistence baseline. You're forecasting 36 minutes; the Sun barely moves in 36 minutes, so this is a strong guess and any error you report is meaningless without it beside it.\n- **how much the flip changed the answer** \u2014 un-flips the flipped prediction and compares it to the upright one. Near 0 means the model is blind to orientation, so Hale's law can't explain the cycle-25 failure. Large means orientation genuinely matters and your hypothesis is live. This is the number your project turns on, and you get it here before any training.\n- **one real training step**, converted to sample-views per GPU-hour, plus peak GPU memory against the card's 46 GB and an echo of `checkpoint_layers`.\n\nIt returns the model to the CPU and empties the CUDA cache at the end, so nothing downstream changes.\n\n## Run order\n\nCells 0\u219227 in order. Cell 29's CPU forward pass is superseded by cell 27 \u2014 skip it; it's the slow one. Cells 30\u201338 (the metrics demos) need `output` and `target` from 29, so either run 29 or skip that whole block too; neither affects training.\n\n## Two things worth knowing\n\n**Your training data never flips.** Cell 11 doesn't pass `flip_probability`, so it stays at its `0.0` default and every sample goes through upright. Add `flip_probability=0.5,` next to `max_number_of_samples=3` when you want the mixed-orientation training your experiment is built around. Cell 27 tests the flip mechanically without needing it.\n\n**`max_number_of_samples=3` means the 3 *earliest* flares** \u2014 the cap is a plain `[:N]` slice of a list sorted by peak time, so those are all from 2010. Fine for a plumbing check, not representative of anything.\n\nTwo config edits I'd make for speed, but they're outside the notebook so they're your call: `configs/config_script.yaml:127` `checkpoint_layers: [0,1,2,3,4]` instead of all ten (cell 27 will tell you if you have the memory headroom), and line 98 `s3_boto3_max_concurrency: 16` instead of 4 to make the cold pass finish sooner."
    },
