      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "Confirmed by grep: **no. Zero flipped images anywhere right now.**\n\n`flip_probability` exists only in `flare_dataset.py:48`, where it defaults to `0.0`. It appears nowhere in the notebook, nowhere in `config_script.yaml`, nowhere in either `configs.py`. So the flip branch at `flare_dataset.py:149` never fires \u2014 every sample goes through upright, and the `was_flipped` key that shows up in every batch is always `False`.\n\nThat's why your run trained fine and told you nothing about orientation: it was an ordinary un-flipped fine-tune.\n\nThe forced-flip cell I added (27) does its own explicit flip on one sample, so it tests the mechanism regardless of this setting. But the *training* had no flips in it.\n\nTurning it on is one line in cell 11:",
