      "body": "The outputs aren't in the notebook \u2014 I ran the same code as a standalone script, so nothing was written back into the `.ipynb`. If you open it now, cells 28\u201329 are there but unexecuted.\n\nTo see it yourself, run these cells in order: **2, 3, 5, 7, 10, 11, 17, 19, 21, 23, 29.** Skip everything else.\n\nIt'll be quicker than my 160 s, because the four files it needs are now in `/home/jovyan/scratch_space/surya_cache` \u2014 the reads that dominated the run are already paid for. Two things to set first:\n\n- Cell 11: `max_number_of_samples=2` to match exactly what I ran. If you leave it at 3, you'll get one extra sample per split that isn't cached yet, so add ~40 s.\n- Cell 29: `RUN_TRAINING_STEP = False` for the minimum. Leave it `True` if you also want part C (the real batches through the training loop with flips on).\n\nWhat you'll see, in order: `Loaded 157 / 159`, then the decoder fix reporting the two copied tensors, then `A. PASS`, then the per-sample table, then the two summary numbers.\n\nIf you'd rather have the run I did saved *in* the notebook as a record so it's visible without re-running, I can write those outputs into cells 23 and 29 \u2014 say the word. Running it yourself is better though: you'll see the timings on your own session, and re-running is the point of a check.",
