      "body": "Patched \u2014 cell 29 now restores `flip_probability` right after part B, in both the early-exit and part-C paths.\n\nOne thing to be clear about: **the measurement did use flipped data.** Part B flips the tensors itself with `torch.flip` inside the loop, which is why the errors differ (`+0.0165`) and why persistence came out bit-identical. What didn't flip was the *plot*, because cell 56 reads fresh from the dataset and the dataset had been left at 0.0. The test was fine; the picture afterwards wasn't.\n\nFor the plots, set it explicitly rather than relying on the restore. `saved_p` is 0.5, so a restored dataset flips at random \u2014 roughly every other read, which is confusing when you're looking at one image:\n\n```python\n# deterministic flipped plot\ntrain_data_loader.dataset.flip_probability = 1.0   # then run cell 56\ntrain_data_loader.dataset.flip_probability = 0.0   # then run cell 56 again\n```\n\nConfirm with the `Flipped?  ->  flare_dataset = True/False` line cell 56 already prints, and put `0.5` back before any training run.",
