      "body": "Created `downstream_apps/flare_forecast/2b_flip_minimal.ipynb` \u2014 17 cells, two markdown (top and bottom), everything else code. Validates, every code cell parses.\n\n| cell | what |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | env vars + all imports |\n| 2 | config |\n| 3 | assets + scalers |\n| **4** | **`FLIP_PROBABILITY` / `N_SAMPLES`** + dataloaders |\n| 5 | build model |\n| 6 | load weights + decoder fix (prints all 159) |\n| 7 | LoRA / freeze (yours, verbatim) |\n| 8 | the four `FlareMetrics` |\n| 9 | `Flare2DLightningModule` (yours, verbatim) |\n| 10 | seed + `lit_model` |\n| 11 | flip check, parts A and B |\n| 12 | set orientation for the plot |\n| 13 | your \"proper image check\" plot (verbatim) |\n| 14 | loggers + trainer |\n| 15 | restore the flip mix, then `trainer.fit` |\n\nFour things I changed rather than copied straight across:\n\n**Cell 12 exists because of the bug you caught.** It sets `flip_probability = 1.0` right before the plot, so the picture is deterministic. Flip it to `0.0` and re-run 13 to get the same flare upright. At 0.5 the plot flips at random, which is what confused things earlier.\n\n**Cell 15 puts the mix back before `fit`**, because cell 12 left it pinned at 1.0. Without that, training would see one orientation only \u2014 the opposite of your experiment.\n\n**Cell 11 restores `flip_probability` itself** now, right after part B, so nothing downstream reads unflipped data by accident.\n\n**Dropped entirely:** the CPU forward pass, the four metrics-demo cells, the speed check, the forced-flip timing cell, and the draft plot. None of them feed anything you need.\n\nTwo notes on running it. Cell 13 is your plot with `STRIDE = 1`, so it transforms full 4096\u00b2 frames \u2014 set `STRIDE = 4` while iterating and it's roughly 16\u00d7 faster. And `N_SAMPLES` has to stay \u2265 2: `batch_size` is 2 with `drop_last=True`, so one sample gives you an empty training loader.",
