    {
      "body": "Yes \u2014 all 13, both for input and for what it predicts, with no masking anywhere. Verified on a real sample:\n\n- **Input** `ts` is `(13, 2, 4096, 4096)` \u2014 13 channels \u00d7 2 input frames. Every channel has a healthy spread (std 0.67\u20130.99), none is all-zero.\n- **Target** `forecast` is `(13, 1, 4096, 4096)` and the head outputs `(1, 13, 4096, 4096)` \u2014 it predicts all 13 too.\n- **The three augmentation knobs that could drop channels are all off**: `num_mask_aia_channels=0`, `drop_hmi_probability=0.0`, `random_vert_flip=False`. The base dataset *can* randomly zero AIA channels and drop HMI during training, but the builder never passes those, so nothing is masked in train or val.\n- **The loss flattens all 13 together** (`preds.reshape(-1)` in `flare_metrics.py`), so overall MSE = the plain mean of the per-channel MSEs \u2014 confirmed numerically: 0.2263 both ways. Every channel gets equal weight.\n\nOne thing in that breakdown is directly relevant to your presentation. The error is not spread evenly at all:\n\n| channel group | share of the loss |\n|---|---|\n| **hmi_bx + hmi_by** | **58.7%** |\n| hmi_m + hmi_bz | 20.6% |\n| aia94 | 10.6% |\n| the other 7 AIA + hmi_v | 10.1% |\n\nNearly **80% of the loss comes from the four HMI magnetic channels** \u2014 and those are exactly the channels where polarity lives, i.e. the ones Hale's law is about. So your flip experiment is being measured mostly on the quantity you care about, which is lucky. It also means a single `val_loss` number is effectively \"how well did it predict the magnetic field,\" and the AIA channels barely register.\n\nTwo consequences worth having ready:\n\n1. If flipping hurts, it will show up in `hmi_bx`/`hmi_by` first. A per-channel version of the flipped-vs-upright comparison would be a much sharper result than the single number.\n2. Surya beats persistence on **every** channel here (e.g. hmi_by 0.87 vs 1.74, aia171 0.012 vs 0.021), and by the widest margin on the magnetic ones. That's a solid headline.\n\nWant me to add the per-channel table as a cell under your \"Extra checks\" heading, so it runs on the trained model and splits by `was_flipped`?",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1789657799.8492475,
      "id": "64740cfb-3926-4e32-9d4e-076bc77fb97f",
      "mentions": [],
      "type": "msg"
    },
    {
      "sender": "jpereira",
      "type": "msg",
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "how big is my training/validation set rn",
      "id": "e0915107-b281-49f6-96a0-405014ead7c7",
      "metadata": {
        "to_persona": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
        "model": {
          "settings": {},
          "id": null
