    {
      "body": "so now coming up with a training/validation/testing experiment for my mini-project for this workshop... what do you recommend? i need a presentation by tomorrow so i want the code to be able to run on like realistic portions but idk how long anything wil take to run anyway? \nthese are the instructions i was given with updated timeline. i know now that both images can get flipped and i can use different timing between inputs but i wanna know what the controls (batch size, epoch???, numebr of workers, and of course number of samples) should be for training/val/test split. can you please assist?\ninstructions:\n\"These are the recommendations I made of the kind of experiments you can run:\n- Runs with different amounts of training data and the same validation.\n- Runs with different training sets and the same validation (build your own ensemble).\n- Baseline and finetuning runs with identical training and validation sets.\n\nMy recommendation is that you have a conversation with claude about a plan to run experiments that achieve any or several of this, given that you have about 24 hours (8 of which you\u2019ll be asleep) and training is slow. \"",
